-- title:
--   A common word bound for the complete source stage
-- statement:
--   For input size $n$, let $m=\lfloor\log_2n\rfloor$, $h$ be the prescribed micro-half, $P$ the prime-window scale, and $M$ the maximum modulus. Use the common resource scale $\Sigma_n=2^{2048(m+1)}+2^{5000000(h+1)^2}+M+P+n+100$.
--
--   Let $r_n$ be the prescribed radix, and let $U\in\mathbb N$ bound input magnitudes. Denote by $W_{\rm source}(n,M,U,r_n)$ the finite word requirement of the source-controls host, including source residue construction, retained-source work, and the source-bank routines. At the prescribed maximum modulus $M$,
--   $$W_{\rm source}(n,M,U,r_n)\le200\Sigma_n^3+4U.$$
--   This holds for every natural $n,U$.
--
--   The estimate combines the separate source routines' numerical requirements into the cubic scale envelope used by the encoded color pipeline.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorSourceResources.lean#L184-L209

